                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c1620a1-9cf5-4d4d-9a86-5796bc1d12de",
                        "source_entry_id": "07d393f6-1195-311c-85b4-b2677e84c7a6",
                        "source_sense_id": "d580fecc-8c01-3ac8-8b57-389903eb4ad9",
                        "target_lang_word": "all-powerful",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "all-powerful",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed15e1a3-8953-390c-a6a1-1976fbb231f9",
                                        "entry_id": "2b173079-d32b-33c4-86e4-34b2681f88eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having unlimited power; omnipotent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95202a6e-ca73-4775-b886-9a3153624a0f",
                                                "sense_id": "ed15e1a3-8953-390c-a6a1-1976fbb231f9",
                                                "text": "Imagination is faithful when it is all-powerful."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad29f0a5-d670-4c91-a45e-492a74b7395e",
                                                "sense_id": "ed15e1a3-8953-390c-a6a1-1976fbb231f9",
                                                "text": "The friendless Italian was a much safer person than the niece of the all-powerful minister, whose ambition would not stop but at the throne. Francesca might be allowed to detach him from Mademoiselle Mancini, and could then be easily flung aside."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b40c001-804d-4c3a-8689-2182f0e24368",
                                                "sense_id": "ed15e1a3-8953-390c-a6a1-1976fbb231f9",
                                                "text": "\"Why, dost thou believe that I, who am all-powerful, I, whose loveliness is more than the loveliness of the Grecian Helen, of whom they used to sing, and whose wisdom is wider, ay, far more wide and deep than the wisdom of Solomon the Wise [...] why, I say, oh stranger, dost thou think that I herd here with barbarians lower than the beasts?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10e5730b-f915-42ed-82bf-85ccb23fd556",
                                                "sense_id": "ed15e1a3-8953-390c-a6a1-1976fbb231f9",
                                                "text": "But in his 1996 novel, Holy Fire, [Bruce] Sterling imagines a rather different future: a world ruled by an all-powerful gerontocracy, which appropriates most of the world's wealth to pay for ever more costly life-extension techniques."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0b4f9192-6885-4814-9c28-33b1a248afb9",
                        "source_entry_id": "07d393f6-1195-311c-85b4-b2677e84c7a6",
                        "source_sense_id": "d580fecc-8c01-3ac8-8b57-389903eb4ad9",
                        "target_lang_word": "omnipotent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "omnipotent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03dfc7d8-4e6d-3d00-bbe6-bbbba32cb4c5",
                                        "entry_id": "37fe40c1-f753-3b3c-9119-d0d180ef661e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having unlimited power, force or authority."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2b97d11-226c-4742-8c32-90d7c76bc6e3",
                                                "sense_id": "03dfc7d8-4e6d-3d00-bbe6-bbbba32cb4c5",
                                                "text": "All the spirits of the elements bowed down before him; but the future was still hidden from his eyes, and Death was omnipotent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc6c9af2-63c1-3db4-a0e0-1d466be1733d",
                                        "entry_id": "37fe40c1-f753-3b3c-9119-d0d180ef661e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Describing a cell (especially a stem cell) that is capable of developing into any type of cell or forming any type of tissue (also called a totipotent cell)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58963d78-1cd6-36c0-b3de-ccd9f2a27c87",
                                        "entry_id": "37fe40c1-f753-3b3c-9119-d0d180ef661e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Arrant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "omnipotent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "621792b1-e539-3ff1-b062-fb3670b13419",
                                        "entry_id": "af72dbb7-33bd-3500-be75-714b279d6a0e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An omnipotent being."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "79277362-aae7-48a3-aff3-03c676c9ebb5",
                        "source_entry_id": "07d393f6-1195-311c-85b4-b2677e84c7a6",
                        "source_sense_id": "d580fecc-8c01-3ac8-8b57-389903eb4ad9",
                        "target_lang_word": "tout-puissant",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tout-puissant",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fdfcd60d-4b23-3f64-bb17-aa389c05a6b0",
                                        "entry_id": "0cf1a2eb-858d-331d-a18e-26d21aed1ec8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Omnipotent, qui a un très grand pouvoir."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ed0c454-aa94-475e-b87f-9702f1f78b3f",
                                                "sense_id": "fdfcd60d-4b23-3f64-bb17-aa389c05a6b0",
                                                "text": "Et tous, me voyant en bons termes avec le maître tout-puissant, sont pour moi pleins d'amabilité et de prévenances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1a000c3-f41f-4fb6-800f-f76f92003325",
                                                "sense_id": "fdfcd60d-4b23-3f64-bb17-aa389c05a6b0",
                                                "text": "De tous ces événements qui lui étaient arrivés, ce qui lui semblait surnager, c’était plus que jamais la nécessité urgente de se mettre sous la sauvegarde d’un tout-puissant protecteur comme Concini, maréchal d’Ancre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdf1f505-c154-4715-80bb-b18aff01c27c",
                                                "sense_id": "fdfcd60d-4b23-3f64-bb17-aa389c05a6b0",
                                                "text": "Pendant ce temps, M. Richard se courbe, fait la révérence, salue, marche à reculons comme s’il avait devant lui ce haut et tout-puissant fonctionnaire qu’est M. le sous-secrétaire d’État aux Beaux-Arts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d1ced77-d444-36d1-bfba-317cb0b4a01a",
                                        "entry_id": "0cf1a2eb-858d-331d-a18e-26d21aed1ec8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a une puissance absolue et illimitée."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0958ffa5-4217-45c0-b822-d6b3ca1fbf5d",
                                                "sense_id": "7d1ced77-d444-36d1-bfba-317cb0b4a01a",
                                                "text": "Descartes a donné trois démonstrations de l’existence de Dieu. nᵒ 1 J’ai en moi l’idée de Dieu. Par le nom de Dieu, j’entends une substance infinie, éternelle, immuable, indépendante, toute-connaissante et toute-puissante."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83cc443a-799f-48f6-9c96-c5a641ae4c45",
                                                "sense_id": "7d1ced77-d444-36d1-bfba-317cb0b4a01a",
                                                "text": "Il est donc légitime lorsque la foi et la raison semblent en désaccord, de tenir pour vraies les affirmations de la foi, puisque le miracle est chose toujours réalisable pour un Dieu tout-puissant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6997d989-33f2-430b-a10c-91a396853319",
                                                "sense_id": "7d1ced77-d444-36d1-bfba-317cb0b4a01a",
                                                "text": "O-se-ki, l’Esprit immanent et tout-puissant, s’appesantissait sur elle. Il était plus redoutable que l’homme et elle n’avait nul moyen de lui échapper. — (James Oliver Curwood, Kazan, 1914, traduit de l’anglais par P. Gruyer et L. Postif, Hachette, 1937, pages 209-210)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eaac1a7e-2946-4a6a-a228-3e7343e75635",
                                                "sense_id": "7d1ced77-d444-36d1-bfba-317cb0b4a01a",
                                                "text": "Les croyants l’écrivent généralement avec une respectueuse majuscule : Tout-puissant."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
